If it doesn't, then something is
wrong.

00:34:53.060 --> 00:34:57.240
The ending result that you find
should involve your entire data

00:34:57.240 --> 00:34:58.040
set.

00:34:58.040 --> 00:35:01.400
That's true now for the constant
model and will also be true when

00:35:01.400 --> 00:35:03.420
we look at the simple linear
regression model.

00:35:03.420 --> 00:35:06.020
Your formulas for your optimal
parameters should involve the

00:35:06.020 --> 00:35:08.000
whole data set.
It shouldn't just have a single

00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:10.600
yi in it.
Because intuitively,

00:35:10.920 --> 00:35:13.960
the optimal parameters should
have, you have to look at the

00:35:13.960 --> 00:35:18.100
whole data set to figure out
what those are.

00:35:18.100 --> 00:35:19.100
OK.

