00:41:09.140 --> 00:41:14.020
But note that the technique for
finding that the median is the

00:41:14.020 --> 00:41:17.520
minimizer can't involve taking
the derivative and setting it

00:41:17.520 --> 00:41:18.940
equal to 0.

00:41:18.940 --> 00:41:22.560
Because at all of these bends,

00:41:22.560 --> 00:41:25.560
the derivative is undefined.

00:41:28.440 --> 00:41:32.190
So minimizer isn't always the
same as derivative equals 0.

00:41:32.200 --> 00:41:34.660
One of the ideas you may have
learned in calculus is that a

00:41:34.660 --> 00:41:38.680
critical point, which is a place
where a minimizer or maximizer

00:41:38.680 --> 00:41:43.180
could be, is anywhere where the
derivative is zero or undefined.

00:41:44.020 --> 00:41:47.300
And the way that I think about
it is that at the bottom is

00:41:47.300 --> 00:41:51.050
where the slope goes from
negative to positive.

00:41:52.640 --> 00:41:56.360
So if you look at the segment to
the left of the median,

00:41:56.360 --> 00:41:59.020
the line is decreasing, and to
the right it is increasing.

00:41:59.020 --> 00:42:00.800
And if you think about that
conceptually,

00:42:00.800 --> 00:42:05.340
what that means is you must be
coming out of a hole

00:42:05.340 --> 00:42:08.340
or of a valley.

00:42:22.980 --> 00:42:23.820
Now,

