00:47:26.700 --> 00:47:29.160
And this is only defined,

00:47:29.160 --> 00:47:32.160
as I said earlier,

00:47:32.800 --> 00:47:37.540
when w is not equal to any of

00:47:37.540 --> 00:47:39.420
the yi's.

00:47:41.060 --> 00:47:44.900
Because when w is equal to any
of the yi's, again, you have to

00:47:44.900 --> 00:47:46.960
think back at that piecewise
linear graph,

00:47:46.960 --> 00:47:47.880
you're at a bend,

00:47:47.880 --> 00:47:51.300
the slope is not defined there.

00:47:51.300 --> 00:47:55.040
Number to the left minus number
to the right over n.

00:47:55.040 --> 00:47:58.240
So this formula will help you
reason about what the height of

00:47:58.240 --> 00:48:01.180
this graph is at any point.

00:48:01.180 --> 00:48:02.720
Okay, and this is the kind of
