00:48:41.740 --> 00:48:42.520
Gustavo.

00:48:42.520 --> 00:48:44.500
It would be negative 4 over n.

00:48:44.500 --> 00:48:45.940
And what is n here?

00:48:45.940 --> 00:48:48.100
n would be 5,

00:48:48.100 --> 00:48:48.940
6.

00:48:48.940 --> 00:48:49.940
6.

00:48:50.480 --> 00:48:51.100
Good.

00:48:51.100 --> 00:48:52.860
How did you find that?

00:48:52.860 --> 00:48:55.900
Because there was one point to
the left If you go to the center

00:48:55.900 --> 00:48:58.220
and there's five points to the
right.

00:48:58.220 --> 00:48:59.100
Remember,

00:48:59.100 --> 00:49:02.020
the formula does not work when
you're exactly on a data point.

00:49:02.020 --> 00:49:05.200
So you just consider an
arbitrary point on the segment.

00:49:05.200 --> 00:49:06.740
So it could be anywhere here.

00:49:06.740 --> 00:49:09.400
If you live here, how many data
points are to the left of you?

00:49:09.400 --> 00:49:10.560
One.
How many are to the right?

00:49:11.100 --> 00:49:11.680
Five.

00:49:11.680 --> 00:49:13.240
And how many are there total?

00:49:13.240 --> 00:49:14.240
Six.

00:49:14.580 --> 00:49:18.020
So I have 1 minus 5 over 6,

00:49:18.020 --> 00:49:20.740
which is negative 2 thirds.

00:49:20.740 --> 00:49:23.480
What this shows you is anytime
you're left of the median, then

00:49:23.480 --> 00:49:28.380
the number of data points to the
left of you is going to be less

00:49:28.380 --> 00:49:29.640
than the number to the right.

00:49:29.640 --> 00:49:31.760
You're less than halfway through
the distribution,

00:49:31.760 --> 00:49:34.020
so you're going to have less to
the left, and so the slope is

00:49:34.020 --> 00:49:35.000
negative.

00:49:35.000 --> 00:49:37.020
As soon as you're halfway
through the data set,

00:49:37.020 --> 00:49:39.120
you're going to have more to the
left, because you will have

00:49:39.120 --> 00:49:40.740
passed more of the data set.

00:49:40.740 --> 00:49:43.380
So left minus right will be
positive, and your slope will be

00:49:43.380 --> 00:49:44.280
positive.

00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:46.880
And that's how we reason about
the median being the minimizer,

00:49:46.880 --> 00:49:50.380
because it's that point at which
you you go from having a

00:49:50.380 --> 00:49:53.360
negative slope to a positive
slope.

00:49:53.360 --> 00:49:54.360
OK?

